Subject: [PATCH 141/148] docs(gastown): describe claim identities for both gc
 1.4.x and 1.5.0 (gcp-fooz4)

P5 follow-up, prose only. Several passages described claim identities as gc
1.4.x recorded them. Under gc 1.5.0 a named seat's BEADS_ACTOR is its
alias, a namepool polecat's BEADS_ACTOR and claim assignee are its alias,
and an unaliased pool session's are its session bead id
(session.AssigneeIdentifier).

- mol-refinery-patrol.toml, the "Claim by writing --assignee=$GC_AGENT"
  paragraph: `--claim` writes $BEADS_ACTOR, which is the runtime session
  name on 1.4.x and the seat's alias, equal to $GC_AGENT, on 1.5.0.
  Writing $GC_AGENT is right on both. No other line in the file changed.
- mol-deacon-patrol.toml: a polecat claim carries whatever form the
  claiming gc recorded (session name on 1.4.x; alias or session bead id
  on 1.5.0).
- polecat prompt, the claim-order sentence: the lookup order (session bead
  ID, runtime session name, then alias) is still what gc 1.5.0's default
  work query uses (internal/config/workquery.go:982-983), so it stays.
  The sentence now adds which identity 1.5.0 records a new claim under.
- polecat prompt, resume re-verify: "Pool restarts mint a NEW session
  identity" is false for a 1.5.0 namepool polecat, whose alias is a chair
  the pool reuses. The same claim, in the live-owner guard comment and in
  both copies of the approval-fallacy guard comment, now reads "usually".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
